For material design choices, explain gains, losses, affected users/team, and fit to known project goals in conversation or handoff, not product UI. Label assumptions; preserve chosen directions.

## Match the requested change

Classify the request as repair, polish, or redesign: restore behavior, refine layout, or rebuild layout and components. Follow the user's scope, not analytics-only tool context. Do not downgrade redesign to polish, expand repair, or turn token export/source inspection into a redesign.

Keep the selected design system and assigned icon family/variant unless the user requests a change. Use exact returned icon names/source, never substitute packs, emoji, or invented SVGs. Inventory sections, components, states and responsive layouts; map requested patterns to real system components and record missing primitives.

Plan structural changes and component adoption before redesigning. Rebuild the requested hierarchy, layout and interactions; token swaps and unused imports do not count. Preserve unrelated behavior, accessibility and production/control boundaries.

Preserve all supplied paragraphs, reviews, offer details, links and disclosures, including collapsed answers and inactive tabs, unless the user requests cuts or rewrites. Require a source-to-render content comparison; investigate every omission, not just section counts. A shortened fixture is not a completed page. Label partial prototypes and never treat their checks as full-page evidence.

Compare before/after renders of the same content and states at the same desktop and mobile widths. Show which planned structural changes and component adoption are visible; verify the selected icons, spacing, hierarchy, and working interactions. Copy and accessibility fixes alone do not complete a redesign. Tool calls, generated files, or a source-only review are not visual evidence. If a baseline or rendered check is unavailable, name the missing evidence and report the redesign as unverified. Keep all existing build, accessibility, hover, comprehension, and review gates.

This design system already selects Feather (default). Do not call `find-icon-library` or choose a substitute. Call `find-icons` with `libraryId: "feather"` and `variant: "default"` for each needed concept, then use the exact returned names and source. Preserve the family, variant, viewBox, fill, stroke, and duotone opacity. If exact material is unavailable, report it; do not guess slugs or draw replacement SVGs.

# Notion

**Description:** Clean light theme with a white page, near-black text, bright blue primary buttons with soft corners, and understated minimal styling
**Personality:** clean, minimal, light, warm, productivity
**Industry:** productivity, saas, tools, education, enterprise
**Primary Color:** oklch(0.568 0.182 254.3)
**Border Radius:** 0.5rem
**Font:** ui-sans-serif, -apple-system, "system-ui", "Segoe UI Variable Display", "Segoe UI", Helvetica, "Apple Color Emoji", Arial, sans-serif
**Preview (see it live):** https://better-design.com/design-systems/notion

## Install just these components

> **Requirements:** these components target **Tailwind v4**. The installed `globals.css` uses the v4 entry point (`@import "tailwindcss"`), so the project needs `tailwindcss@^4` with `@tailwindcss/postcss` in its PostCSS config (or the `@tailwindcss/vite` plugin). On a Tailwind v3 project, migrate to v4 first, otherwise the build throws the "trying to use tailwindcss directly as a PostCSS plugin" error.

```bash
# Init shadcn if missing (idempotent, skips when components.json exists)
[ -f components.json ] || npx shadcn@latest init -d -y

npx shadcn@latest add \
  https://better-design.com/registry/notion/input.json \
  https://better-design.com/registry/notion/typography.json \
  https://better-design.com/registry/notion/button-base.json \
  https://better-design.com/registry/notion/card.json \
  https://better-design.com/registry/notion/sidebar.json
```

_This installs the Base UI flavor where available, plus plain registry entries for components without a Base UI twin. If the project uses Radix, re-run this tool with `library: "radix"` instead._

**Run the install. Do not substitute it.** Never hand-write these components from memory and never build a standalone HTML mockup as a stand-in: both skip the real design tokens, drift from the registry source, and cannot `import` from `@/components/ui/*`. The only correct output is running the command above in a real project, then composing the installed files.

